We consider the Diophantine equation
\begin{equation*}
y^{2}=(36n^{3}-19-12mn)^{2}-(2m)^{3}.
\end{equation*}

The trivial family is \(m=0\), \(y=\pm(36n^{3}-19)\). All solutions listed
below are nontrivial (\(m\neq 0\)). Each row represents the two signed
solutions \((n,m,\pm|y|)\); the table thus gives \(39\) nontrivial
\((n,m,|y|)\)-triples, i.e.\ \(78\) signed nontrivial integer solutions.
Rows marked \(\star\) are new relative to the original \(29\)-row table.

